// A lambda's body is ordinary code, lowered in the module the lambda is
// WRITTEN in -- so it may not reach another module's private function. If it
// could, a lambda would be a way around `pub`: write one here, call the
// private function from it, and hand the interface to anyone.
import lib;

lib.Less l = (lib.Point a, lib.Point b) => lib.by_y(a, b);
print(l.cmp(lib.Point(3, 9), lib.Point(1, 5)));
